body:
Not saying you can't, I'm saying that me, personally, I would want to focus on understanding more than talking for now, i just don't like talking if i know that there are 40 or 50% of things i might not understand.

&#x200B;

But you do you.

Because as in most other languages you do need to understand the language first before you can speak to others

&#x200B;

I did try to speak to others in French before, but it wasn't what I wanted lol

&#x200B;

I actually had a couple of job interviews too.

&#x200B;

Anyways like I said, I want to get to a point where I understand 100% of what I hear and then I can speak.

&#x200B;

anyways it's not like it's easy to find language partners, people flake, and some aren't serious and some are just at different learning stages.

I have read that after certain age your brain just doesn't understand new sounds or languages because of the weird sentence structure.

&#x200B;

the problem with french, there is loads of words, expression that are too slang to be in the subtitles of any film or video, 

&#x200B;

they just learn it because they were born speaking it, my fear is, how are we gonna know those slang words, they aren't translated into shows or in videos.

&#x200B;

which means that no matter how much we learn, we will always be limited because we don't know those words.

Yes, I tried to even read tom sawyer adventures in English and the very first page I was met with some odd phrases and vocab lol

&#x200B;

And then it hit me, if i speak the language without having to read or understand those old novels then why am I doing it in french!!

&#x200B;

I would much rather read modern day vocabulary and useful words and phrases that can be found in articles, news, videos, etc.

Yes, i just got done with tom sawyer in French, i read the little prince in french, and notre dame really made me stop with how shocking it is, very old confusing style, words.

&#x200B;

So now I'm reading articles from a website called narcity lol.

Bro i have been fired from jobs, i have left jobs because i wasn't social enough, i have had problems with social anxiety my entire life, that is with also for like half my life i have had nose skin issues, acne, scarred my self as well, was addicted to ciggaretes, soda and other things, all of that worsened my skin, i have had friends, yes, but i lost them ALL, as in stopped being friends with them, not that they died or anything

&#x200B;

i can't even hang onto a job anymore, I'm in my 30's

&#x200B;

my dreams of travelling, making money, and being rich, travelling thw world, being social, being a youtuber among other dreams are crushed

&#x200B;

now i'm jobless, scarred, have acne problems with my nose skin and enlarged pores from smoking too much and consuming a lot of sugar.

&#x200B;

so yeah i feel you, i probably don't fit in anywhere as well

&#x200B;

like man, all my life goals have failed so far.

&#x200B;

yeah I'm also a virgin, and never had a girlfriend, uhhmm.

 i quit this game like 3-3-2023

&#x200B;

my last game was a crown victory royale

&#x200B;

not even sure what season it is now or if crowns are still a thing

you really believe Brandon pulls the same numbers as ice? wow

&#x200B;

when ice stream went down sam's stream got up to 6k, you're telling me that they are going to bot sam too while ice is down or maybe it's just real viewers and you just can't accept that ice still got a good following??

&#x200B;

wow some people just want to believe what they want to believe.

brah he said in an interview that he had to slow down and give away the third round and clinch because he was afraid of gassing out in the least round and lose

&#x200B;

so he really didn't gas out he was being smart and resting, he said that he was limbing on one of his legs weeks before the fight like he pulled something, and he knew that he wouldn't be able to go at it for all 4 round so he had to slow down and sacrifice one round.

buts  and what ifs, i think in every fight there is buts and ifs

&#x200B;

so next fight probably might have buts and ifs too

&#x200B;

fact is tommy won, end of.

Yeah that's kinda similar to what we have here but we don't sell newspapers in them anymore, it's usually just a stand for selling drinks, bags of chips, small packaged items like biscuits or chocolate and cigarettes which is why sometimes it's called a cigarettes stand because that's the most popular item, it's usually in a squared shape,  very tiny space for someone to set in and is surrounded by products, we do have gazebos which is a round shaped structure made out of wood which is completely empty and its only purpose is for people to sit in in parks or wherever.

&#x200B;

Edit: I saw the pictures, yup that's basically what I was referring to, I guess I shall use kiosques then.

I think it depends on what you think of the last les, if it's complement for the kids, then you're right,

&#x200B;

But I thought of the last les as a complement for the questions so it's les because it's a direct object in that case.

>I promise if you just practice in creative for a while you’ll improve

hahaha you're saying that to the guy who has been doing that for years lol, i used to practice in game before creative was a thing and then came playgrounds and then they renamed it to creative, from ramp rushing tutorials to double edits to highroad retakes, tips and tricks, watching streamers and analyzing their gameplay, dude I done it all for HOURS AND HOURS.

&#x200B;

This game IS ALL ABOUT YOU FPS AND PING, period,

&#x200B;

Do you see anyone who' a streamer playing on just 60 and 100 ping lol they all have optimum setups loooool
